It contains no third-party source code. Algorithms taken from published work
(online softmax, FlashAttention tiling, the int8-to-fp16 magic-number
conversion, split-KV with log-sum-exp combine) are re-implemented from the
papers, the PTX ISA and the CUDA programming guide.

References: Milakov & Gimelshein, arXiv:1805.02867 (online softmax); Dao et
al., arXiv:2205.14135, and Dao, arXiv:2307.08691 (FlashAttention and
FlashAttention-2); Dao, Haziza, Massa & Sizov, "Flash-Decoding for long-context
inference", 2023 (split-KV with a log-sum-exp combine); Kim et al.,
arXiv:2211.10017 (the int8-to-fp16 magic-number conversion); Granlund &
Montgomery, PLDI 1994, and the FastDivmod idea of NVIDIA CUTLASS (BSD-3-Clause;
no code copied) for division by a run-time divisor.

At run time the library links against PyTorch (BSD-3-Clause) through its
stable C ABI and the CUDA runtime (NVIDIA CUDA EULA), and the vLLM plugin
imports vLLM (Apache-2.0). None of them is redistributed here.
